7-29\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,2\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429050 #edb/ref 1030 0.5 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186429050 #edb/ref 1032 "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account foundations: 1 rises / 2 eligible passed source activities = 0.500000; nearest selected fraction = 1/2. Crossing activity numbers [2]; waits [2]. Separate account estimates: foundations=1/2 (1/2). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: True. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-report.md. Evidence: reference/mathacademy/encompassing-analysis-2026-10-11/frequency-fractions/foundations-frequency-estimates.json, pair 338->305. All account evidence retained in the prepared import's selected-relationships.json." #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186429050 #edb/ref 1036 #edb/ref 17592186050789 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186429051 #edb/ref 1030 1.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186429051 #edb/ref 1032 "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account foundations: 1 rises / 1 eligible passed source activities = 1.000000; nearest selected fraction = 1. Crossing activity numbers [1]; waits [1]. Separate account estimates: foundations=1 (1/1). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: False. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-report.md. Evidence: reference/mathacademy/encompassing-analysis-2026-10-11/frequency-fractions/foundations-frequency-estimates.json, pair 338->3